# W38-2 — A/B sweep for PixelLossDispatch (AlwaysOn / Auto / AlwaysOff)

date_utc:          2026-05-18T17:30:00Z
host:              lilith (AMD Ryzen 9 7950X, 128 GB)
os:                Linux 6.6 WSL2
git_base:          a2cd4758 (main: bench(lossy): W38 — low-effort phase baseline)
branch_workspace:  ~/work/zen/jxl-encoder--pixel-loss-dispatch
reproducer:
  cargo run -p jxl-encoder --release --features 'std parallel butteraugli-loop' \
    --example pixel_loss_dispatch_ab -- \
    --out benchmarks/pixel_loss_dispatch_2026-05-19.tsv

sweep_grid:
  sources:          5 CID22-512 photos + 3 gb82-sc screenshots = 8 images
  distances:        {0.5, 1.0, 2.0}
  efforts:          {5, 7}
  dispatches:       {AlwaysOn, Auto, AlwaysOff}
  runs_per_cell:    3 (median wall-clock reported, min also captured)
  total_cells:      144  (432 encodes)

sources_photos (CID22-512/validation):
  1025469.png  512x512
  1044329.png  512x512
  1189261.png  512x512
  1279330.png  512x512
  1418519.png  512x512
sources_screen (gb82-sc):
  codec_wiki.png  variable
  imac_g3.png     variable
  terminal.png    variable

dispatch_definitions:
  AlwaysOn (default):
    Always compute mask1x1 + use pixel-domain loss term in
    estimate_entropy_full when ac_strategy_enabled &&
    pixel_domain_loss are both true. Byte-identical to historical
    encoder builds (hash-lock 36/36 verified).
  AlwaysOff:
    Force-skip mask1x1 (equivalent to with_pixel_domain_loss(false)).
    AC strategy search uses coefficient-domain entropy only.
  Auto:
    Compute mask1x1, measure per-image median; when median > 80
    (PIXEL_LOSS_DISPATCH_MEDIAN_THRESHOLD), drop mask1x1 before the
    AC-strategy search. Bitstream-affecting on gated cells; matches
    AlwaysOn behaviour otherwise.

metric_methodology:
  encode_ms:   3-run median wall-clock (default-features build,
               release profile, NOT -C target-cpu=native — runtime
               SIMD dispatch).
  bytes:       jxl-encoder output size (full container + codestream).
  butteraugli: Rust butteraugli_linear, jxl-oxide linear-sRGB decode
               (CLAUDE.md PNG-metadata-immune path).
  ssim2:       fast_ssim2::compute_ssimulacra2, sRGB u8 inputs after
               linear→sRGB conversion of the jxl-oxide decode.

key_findings:
  - Default AlwaysOn byte-identical confirmed: hash_lock_features
    36/36 + test_pixel_loss_dispatch_default_byte_identical_to_explicit_always_on
    pass.
  - photo e5: Auto skips 6/15 cells (per-image median(mask1x1) > 80
    on smooth photos). Wall-clock median Δ vs AlwaysOn = +2.2%
    (computing mask1x1 + then dropping it adds overhead when the
    AlwaysOn path would have used it anyway).
  - screen e5: Auto skips 9/9 cells. Wall-clock median Δ = -1.2%
    vs AlwaysOn. AlwaysOff median Δ = -10.4% — the win when you
    can skip mask1x1 compute too.
  - photo e7 / screen e7: gates fire same ratio; wall-clock Δ
    smaller because pixel_domain_loss is a smaller % of e7's
    deeper AC-strategy search budget.
  - Quality on skipped cells: photo ssim2 median Δ = -0.27 to -0.36;
    screen ssim2 median Δ = -0.64 (e5) / +0.02 (e7). Auto-default
    flip requires a wider corpus + RD-pareto bench (chunk-2 plan).

chunk_2_plan_default_on_auto_flip:
  - 50+ CID22 photos + 20+ gb82-sc screenshots × 5 distances ×
    {AlwaysOn, Auto} × {e5, e7, e8} grid.
  - Per-image RD-pareto comparison: does Auto stay within +/- 1
    ssim2 point and +/- 3% bytes vs AlwaysOn?
  - If yes: flip default to Auto, rebake hash-locks, ship as chunk
    2 with updated baseline.
  - If photos regress >1 ssim2 point on > 5% of cells: keep
    AlwaysOn default, document Auto as opt-in for screen-heavy /
    smooth-photo workloads where the wall-clock win justifies the
    small quality cost.

ranked_per_class_observations_for_chunk2_design:
  photos:
    - Auto skip rate varies image-to-image. 1279330.png skipped
      every distance; 1025469.png/1044329.png/1189261.png never
      skipped at d=0.5/d=1 (median below 80 — textured content).
    - On skipped cells bytes Δ = +5.6% (we LOSE bytes — strategy
      search shifts toward DCT8 without the loss term, smaller
      strategies more often).
    - Auto on photos is a small wall-clock pessimisation on
      non-skipped cells (mask1x1 compute is small but not free).
  screens:
    - 9/9 cells skip — gb82-sc median(mask1x1) sits well above 80.
    - Wall-clock saving is real but smaller than AlwaysOff
      (mask1x1 compute is the residual cost).
    - Quality regresses ~0.6 ssim2 at e5 — likely DCT2x2/IDENTITY
      strategy picks drift without the pixel-loss tiebreaker.
      Worth investigating whether the threshold should be tighter
      for screen content (raise to 100 or 110) so only the
      flattest screens skip.
